7. Third-party components

7.1 The Software includes components made by third parties, each under its own licence. These
    components and their licences are listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt, which comes with the
    Software. For those components, their own licences apply, and nothing in this licence
    limits the rights that those licences give You.

7.2 Some of these components are libraries under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL),
    among them Qt and Qt for Python (PySide6 and Shiboken6) under LGPL version 3, and GEOS
    under LGPL version 2.1. They are included as separate library files. You may modify these
    libraries, replace them in Your installation with modified versions, and reverse engineer
    the Software as far as needed to debug such modifications. Where the licence of such a
    library requires it, You may also modify the Software for Your own use and reverse
    engineer it to debug such modifications, to the extent that licence requires. Sections 5
    and 6 do not restrict these rights. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt states where to obtain the
    source code of these libraries.


8. Updates, licence versions and privacy

8.1 The Software can check for updates. The first time You start it, it asks whether it may do
    so automatically; You can change this in the settings at any time, and the Software asks
    You before it installs an update. To check, it contacts GitHub (github.com), a service of
    GitHub, Inc. Like any internet request, this gives GitHub Your IP address and technical
    information about the request, such as the version of the Software. GitHub handles this
    information under its own privacy statement. The update check sends no other information
    about You or Your work, and the Author receives no personal data from it: GitHub shows the
    Author only overall statistics, such as how often each release file has been downloaded.
    Apart from update checks and web pages that You choose to open, the Software does not
    connect to the internet and does not collect usage data.

8.2 Each copy of the Software comes with the licence version that applies to it, in the file
    LICENSE.txt. Updates and new versions are covered by this licence unless they come with a
    different licence version.

8.3 If an update or new version comes with a different licence version, its release notes say
    so, and the new licence version is available on the website (section 13) before You
    install it. By installing or using the update or version, You accept that licence version
    for it. If You do not accept it, do not install it: You may keep using the version that You
    have, under the licence version that came with it.

8.4 A new licence version never takes away rights that You have under an earlier licence
    version for the versions of the Software that came with it. The licence for a version has
    no end date; it ends only as set out in section 11. All licence versions remain available
    on the website.


