To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Author is not liable for any damage arising
from the use of, or the inability to use, the Software or its Output, including loss or
corruption of data, loss of profits and indirect damage. This does not exclude or limit:
liability that cannot be excluded or limited under applicable law; liability for damage
caused intentionally, through deliberate recklessness or through gross negligence on the part
of the Author; liability for death or personal injury; or liability under mandatory product
liability or consumer protection law. In all other cases in which the Author is nevertheless
liable, the Author's total liability towards You is limited to EUR 100.


11. Termination

11.1 If You breach this licence, the Author may notify You of the breach in writing (email is
     enough). If the breach can be remedied, for example by obtaining a separate licence,
     stopping use that is not covered or restoring removed notices, You have 30 days after the
     notice to remedy it. If You do not, this licence ends at the end of those 30 days.

11.2 The Author may end this licence with immediate effect, by written notice, if the breach
     cannot be remedied, if it is serious and deliberate (such as selling the Software or
     distributing modified copies of it), or if You repeat a breach after an earlier notice.

11.3 You may end this licence at any time by stopping all use of the Software and deleting it.

11.4 When this licence ends, You must stop using the Software and delete or uninstall all
     copies of it that You have. Your Output remains Yours: You may keep Your project files and
     other Output, and continue to publish, sell, license and otherwise use it, as set out in
     sections 2.5(d) and 4.

11.5 You may still ask the Author for a separate licence after this licence has ended. The end
     of this licence does not affect the rights that the Author has under the law for use of
     the Software that was not covered by a licence.

11.6 Sections 2.5(d), 2.7(c), 4, 7, 9, 10, 11.4, 11.5 and 12 continue to apply after this
     licence ends.


12. Governing law and disputes

12.1 This licence is governed by the laws of the Netherlands. If You are a consumer (a natural
     person acting for purposes outside Your trade, business, craft or profession), this does
     not take away the protection that the mandatory law of the country where You live gives
     You.

12.2 Disputes between the Author and anyone who is not a consumer go to the competent court in
     the district of Oost-Brabant (Rechtbank Oost-Brabant), the Netherlands, unless mandatory
     law says otherwise.

12.3 If You are a consumer, section 12.2 does not apply. Disputes then go to the court that
     has jurisdiction under the applicable rules (within the European Union: Regulation (EU)
     No 1215/2012), which may be a court in the country where You live.


